WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:08.500
<b>Aleksandrovsk-Sakhalinsky
(Ako)</b>

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:14.800
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:02:18.670 --> 00:02:24.510
<b>Episode Thirty-Three
Revolutionary</b>

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:30.490
He seems to speak a bit of Russian.

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:39.930
She came here with three men to 
deliver a reindeer, he says.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:41.990
Asirpa-san!

00:02:45.740 --> 00:02:48.910
Lieutenant Koito! Come back!

00:02:49.360 --> 00:02:51.380
They'll let us rest in their tent!

00:02:55.280 --> 00:02:56.810
I saw a tiny reindeer!

00:02:56.810 --> 00:02:58.150
I see.

00:02:58.570 --> 00:03:01.990
Why not put a reindeer bridle
on the Lieutenant here?

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:08.180
Sugimoto, you're a nasty man.

00:03:08.180 --> 00:03:09.040
Right, Tsukishima?

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:12.780
Right, Tsukishima?!

00:03:13.210 --> 00:03:14.710
Tsukishima?!

00:03:21.490 --> 00:03:23.720
<i>We're almost to Ako Prison.</i>

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:26.400
<i>Asirpa-san should be close.</i>

00:03:28.490 --> 00:03:36.000
<b>Ako: Nivkh Village</b>

00:03:29.940 --> 00:03:34.270
The Nivkh are the most populous 
ethnic minority in Karafuto.

00:03:34.270 --> 00:03:39.470
They live a life very similar to the 
Karafuto Ainu, centered around fishing.

00:03:40.710 --> 00:03:42.280
That hat is awesome!

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:44.030
It's got ears!

00:03:48.130 --> 00:03:50.540
If we can get this woman 
who knows so much about

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:54.030
Asirpa-chan's father, Sofia, out of jail,

00:03:54.030 --> 00:03:57.250
we might be able to find out something 
about the code for the gold,

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:58.710
is what you're saying?

00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:05.130
I'm not saying it's impossible, but it feels 
like the risk isn't worth the reward.

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:09.630
Dozens of Sofia's men are 
locked up in Ako Prison.

00:04:09.630 --> 00:04:14.480
They're all allies who fought with me 
for independence for far east minorities.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:16.120
I see.

00:04:16.120 --> 00:04:18.480
And so we want them on our side?

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:22.890
If we find the gold with their help,

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.950
will that really benefit the Ainu?

00:04:26.320 --> 00:04:27.830
Of course.

00:04:28.340 --> 00:04:32.360
It'll benefit not just the Ainu, 
but the Nivkh and the Uilta, too.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.620
The Nanai, the Evenki, the Yakuts...

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:39.090
Every minority that lives in Karafuto 
and far eastern Russia will be

00:04:39.090 --> 00:04:41.930
able to remain who they are.

00:05:41.290 --> 00:05:43.460
Nivkh clothing?

00:05:56.770 --> 00:06:01.710
<b>Vladivostok</b>

00:06:10.840 --> 00:06:12.350
It ran.

00:06:12.350 --> 00:06:16.090
That's rare, to see one so 
close to where humans live.

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:25.230
Hasegawa Photographers

00:06:25.920 --> 00:06:27.650
I'm back, Fina.

00:06:27.800 --> 00:06:29.970
Welcome home, Kouichi.

00:06:30.470 --> 00:06:33.430
Have you been good, Olga?

00:06:34.470 --> 00:06:36.160
You have a guest.

00:06:38.840 --> 00:06:42.760
Hello. I am Hasegawa.

00:06:45.980 --> 00:06:48.470
We haven't come to have our photo taken.

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:52.650
We heard there was a Japanese here.

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:54.720
We're interested in Japan.

00:06:54.720 --> 00:07:00.120
We want you to teach us Japanese. 
Of course, we'll pay.

00:07:02.010 --> 00:07:07.440
Hasegawa-san went to Russia in his teens,
 as part of his dad's job.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:10.490
An acquaintance gave him that 
photographer's studio,

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:13.200
and he began to work as a 
photographer in Vladivostok,

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:15.370
marrying a local woman.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.950
Perhaps he was happy to get a chance 
to speak his old language again,

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:21.750
because he agreed to teach us.

00:07:22.300 --> 00:07:25.500
We learned Japanese from him.

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:30.590
We hid at a local farmer's house 
while visiting his studio,

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:34.510
in what was a brief respite from 
the ten years we spent on the run

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:37.910
for killing the emperor.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:41.770
Sofia treated me like a little brother.

00:07:42.200 --> 00:07:45.690
Me like fat chicks!

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:49.540
You prefer plump women, I see.

00:07:51.010 --> 00:07:51.880
Poop.

00:07:52.410 --> 00:07:53.490
Poop?

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:57.740
You shouldn't talk like that,
 Zoya-san. It's rude.

00:07:57.740 --> 00:07:59.120
Poop bad!

00:07:59.560 --> 00:08:00.380
Poop!

00:08:00.380 --> 00:08:01.370
Poop bad!

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:02.030
Poop!

00:08:02.030 --> 00:08:03.750
Stop it. Both of you.

00:08:04.870 --> 00:08:08.750
Hey. You two. Call it off.

00:08:08.750 --> 00:08:12.370
Harmony is the most critical 
thing in all affairs, right?

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:20.270
Those two men are amazing. They're picking
 up Japanese with amazing speed.

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:24.190
Especially Grigori-san... 
He's frighteningly smart.

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:28.630
Zoya-san doesn't seem cut out for Japanese.

00:08:29.750 --> 00:08:34.510
It's not her intelligence. 
She's just not interested in it.

00:08:46.780 --> 00:08:51.880
Hoinu not like water. Will travel above this.

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:53.670
Pelts sell for a lot.

00:08:55.060 --> 00:08:59.220
Maybe I should set a lot of traps 
like that and buy a new camera, then.

00:09:00.410 --> 00:09:03.810
You shouldn't count your 
hoinu before they hatch.

00:09:04.390 --> 00:09:06.570
When did you learn a phrase like that?

00:09:12.620 --> 00:09:15.490
<i>They're constantly watching 
the area around them.</i>

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:16.710
Wolf...

00:09:21.170 --> 00:09:24.580
That's the same wolf I saw 
the day you came here.

00:09:25.730 --> 00:09:28.330
Wolves are beautiful.

00:09:29.040 --> 00:09:31.890
They lead strong lives, with nothing wasted.

00:09:31.890 --> 00:09:33.740
That's what makes them beautiful.

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:37.840
Beauty and strength are the same.

00:09:38.440 --> 00:09:44.370
But if a wolf is alone, that means 
there's something wrong with it.

00:09:45.070 --> 00:09:50.110
It couldn't get along with its comrades,
 and left or was kicked out.

00:09:51.040 --> 00:09:53.860
You know a lot about the mountains.

00:09:54.210 --> 00:09:59.240
You won't tell me a word about 
where you really came from.

00:10:00.320 --> 00:10:04.880
But you're not from 
the nobility, like Zoya-san.

00:10:05.510 --> 00:10:09.630
She's dressed like a peasant, 
but can read and write Russian.

00:10:09.630 --> 00:10:12.880
And occasionally, she speaks in French.

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:14.990
Here.

00:10:15.920 --> 00:10:16.860
Merci.

00:10:20.670 --> 00:10:25.780
A lot of Russia's upper classes prefer 
to speak in French rather than Russian.

00:10:25.780 --> 00:10:30.310
I think Hasegawa-san had a 
good idea of who she was.

00:10:31.000 --> 00:10:34.730
In those days, some Russian nobles 
and intellectuals would dress

00:10:34.730 --> 00:10:38.390
as peasants and live among them,

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:43.670
attempting to modernize the 
state and overthrow the emperor.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:48.090
Hasegawa-san may have 
known who we were, too.

00:11:05.060 --> 00:11:07.970
<b>Golden Kamuy</b>

00:11:08.930 --> 00:11:13.900
The Russian Empire has always 
had what are called "serfs."

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:16.980
They're halfway between 
a farmer and a slave.

00:11:17.320 --> 00:11:19.910
They had no rights at all.

00:11:20.530 --> 00:11:24.390
Sofia and other revolutionaries 
tried to get them to rise up.

00:11:24.390 --> 00:11:26.240
But they refused.

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:31.620
The revolutionaries decided this was because

00:11:31.620 --> 00:11:38.180
the religious beliefs they held deeply 
were tied to worship of the emperor.

00:11:39.430 --> 00:11:42.040
There was no choice but to prove 
that the emperor was a mere mortal,

00:11:42.040 --> 00:11:45.140
and not a representative of God.

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:48.140
And that line of thought 
lead to his assassination.

00:11:51.290 --> 00:11:55.450
The ethnic minorities consider 
Russia a serious threat.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:59.190
"Our kamuy are being 
replaced by something else.

00:11:59.800 --> 00:12:04.600
Someday we'll be turned into pious 
believers who never complain."

00:12:05.020 --> 00:12:09.440
That's why Wilk and I joined 
her revolutionaries.

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:17.250
And Sofia planned to 
fight alongside us, too.

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:24.690
Ookubo Toshimichi is considered a cruel man

00:12:24.690 --> 00:12:27.640
for his willingness to do whatever 
it took to achieve his goals,

00:12:27.640 --> 00:12:30.900
but he was also a man capable of making 
firm decisions and acting on them.

00:12:31.890 --> 00:12:33.730
His polar opposite was Kido Takayoshi:

00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:36.310
cheerful, logical, flexible.

00:12:36.310 --> 00:12:39.380
A master of the sword who stood 
up against tremendous power.

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:43.570
Saigou Takamori was loyal, kind, 
and had a strong sense of duty.

00:12:43.570 --> 00:12:47.640
An excellent military leader 
who inspired great loyalty.

00:12:48.390 --> 00:12:54.620
These three were the men at the 
core of the Meiji Restoration.

00:12:54.950 --> 00:13:00.380
Thanks to their efforts, Japan was the one 
nation in Asia that was able to modernize.

00:13:05.050 --> 00:13:07.640
Head back to your parents for a while.

00:13:07.990 --> 00:13:11.990
Don't come back until I come to get you.

00:13:13.540 --> 00:13:16.410
Promise me you won't come back.

00:13:19.130 --> 00:13:21.690
I think we're ready to head for Japan.

00:13:22.610 --> 00:13:26.280
But I think she's still uncertain.

00:13:28.030 --> 00:13:31.030
If you tell her to come with you, she will.

00:14:00.920 --> 00:14:02.910
Hasegawa-san, hello.

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:05.980
Please give us another lesson.

00:14:07.130 --> 00:14:09.380
You can't come here anymore.

00:14:09.380 --> 00:14:11.200
Leave. Now.

00:14:15.060 --> 00:14:17.060
Are you Hasegawa Kouichi?

00:14:17.060 --> 00:14:20.630
No, Hasegawa is out.

00:14:20.630 --> 00:14:22.380
And who are you?

00:14:22.380 --> 00:14:28.380
His assistant. What do you want?

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:26.630
The secret police.

00:14:45.100 --> 00:14:46.420
We're surrounded.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:07.950
How many of you came here?

00:15:07.950 --> 00:15:09.820
How many are outside?

00:15:19.750 --> 00:15:21.190
Who are you people?

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:25.680
We came for the Japanese.

00:15:35.680 --> 00:15:42.290
We'd spent months together, and had no 
clue that Hasegawa-san was a Japanese spy.

00:15:43.290 --> 00:15:44.970
His wife didn't either, I'm sure.

00:15:51.550 --> 00:15:54.970
Leave now if you don't want to die!

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:07.080
Come upstairs, please.

00:16:15.690 --> 00:16:18.660
You hid this in your cameras!

00:16:19.060 --> 00:16:21.660
It's ready. Go ahead.

00:16:43.040 --> 00:16:44.470
Don't let a single one get away.

00:16:44.470 --> 00:16:46.980
If they do, they'll come 
back with their friends!

00:17:27.730 --> 00:17:31.880
A single bullet hit the 
baby and the wife at once.

00:17:36.920 --> 00:17:37.680
Fina!

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:44.660
It's no good.

00:17:49.470 --> 00:17:54.610
Go. You have to get as far away 
from here as possible, I'm sure.

00:17:56.410 --> 00:17:57.900
Hasegawa-san!

00:17:58.330 --> 00:18:00.010
Go. Now.

00:18:08.960 --> 00:18:11.390
That was the last we saw of him.

00:18:16.780 --> 00:18:19.160
Sophia blamed herself.

00:18:19.420 --> 00:18:21.370
I told her that the bullet that killed

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:23.900
the baby might've been mine,
 but it didn't help.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:30.450
If there are warrants coming out 
this far, we can't use any port.

00:18:30.870 --> 00:18:33.170
It'll be hard to get into Japan.

00:18:33.170 --> 00:18:35.170
<b>Vladivostok</b>

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:35.990
We'll go further north.

00:18:37.500 --> 00:18:39.550
And then what?

00:18:40.570 --> 00:18:42.790
I have an idea.

00:18:47.260 --> 00:18:49.890
What we've been waiting for is here.

00:18:52.250 --> 00:18:54.660
We've been waiting for the ice floes.

00:18:55.880 --> 00:19:01.910
The Strait of Tartary will be covered in 
ice soon, connecting us to Karafuto.

00:19:03.190 --> 00:19:06.610
We'll walk over the ice to reach Karafuto.

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:08.820
We can get there in a day.

00:19:09.660 --> 00:19:12.650
I got some information from 
the Russian government.

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:16.840
We need to go to Hokkaido 
and see if it's true.

00:19:19.690 --> 00:19:21.050
What's wrong, Sofia?

00:19:21.450 --> 00:19:23.480
I can't go.

00:19:25.030 --> 00:19:27.810
Because Wilk, I love you.

00:19:30.370 --> 00:19:35.790
I can't get the baby I killed out of my head.

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:44.590
I don't need a woman's happiness. 
I'll fight here, as a revolutionary.

00:19:49.210 --> 00:19:51.360
We'll meet again, Sofia.

00:20:02.150 --> 00:20:04.930
Keep safe, kid.

00:20:17.830 --> 00:20:21.090
Did you tell Sofia what happened to Aca?

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:27.950
Wilk...

00:20:31.870 --> 00:20:36.610
Once we get her out, 
we'll head over the ice to Russia,

00:20:36.610 --> 00:20:40.480
and meet up with her allies there.

00:20:52.050 --> 00:20:52.950
Fina...

00:20:58.490 --> 00:20:59.860
Kouichi...

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:08.550
My name isn't Hasegawa Kouichi.

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:13.120
Who are you?

00:21:17.630 --> 00:21:19.270
Tsurumi Tokushirou.

00:23:35.050 --> 00:23:40.250
<b>Next Time
Catching Up to the Wolf</b>

00:23:35.760 --> 00:23:39.980
Next time: "Catching up to the Wolf."
